  <h2>Start with the customer and the studio movement</h2>
  <p>“Pilates wear” is a useful shopping phrase, but it is not a technical specification. A buyer sourcing reformer or mat Pilates clothing should decide how much coverage, compression and visual styling the customer expects. A close-fitting top may stay put during bending and rotation; a looser layer may serve the journey to and from class. Leggings, flare pants and shorts create different movement and styling experiences. Choose the collection deliberately instead of applying one fabric or silhouette to every item.</p>
  <p>For a first private label capsule, specify a core top and bottom before adding many colors. A <a href="/products/tz2557-6/">seamless halter tank and flare leggings set, TZ2557-6</a>, offers one visual direction. A <a href="/products/tz4510-14/">three-piece jacket, bra and leggings set, TZ4510-14</a>, is a different direction when an outer layer matters. These are examples of existing styles, not claims that either design suits every class or customer.</p>

  <h2>Write a sample brief that a manufacturer can actually use</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>What the buyer should specify</th><th>What to check on a sample</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Top</td><td>Tank, bra or long sleeve; neckline; strap and back shape; desired coverage</td><td>Movement at shoulders and chest; whether hem and straps stay in place</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Bottom</td><td>Legging, flare, capri or short; rise; waistband; inseam</td><td>Coverage in forward bend, waistband stability and hem position</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fabric</td><td>Hand feel, stretch, recovery, weight and color direction</td><td>Opacity under stretch, surface appearance, comfort and wash behavior</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sizes</td><td>Target market, base size, grade rules and size quantities</td><td>Fit on more than one body and consistency across the size run</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Branding</td><td>Logo artwork and position, labels, hang tags and packaging</td><td>Appearance and durability after the agreed care test</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>A photo alone cannot communicate waistband tension, fabric recovery or how a top behaves when the wearer bends. Include front and back references, target measurements, and the intended selling position. The <a href="/blogs/activewear-tech-pack-template-specification-sheet/">activewear tech pack template</a> can organize these requirements when a custom design is involved.</p>

  <h2>Ready stock or a custom Pilates clothing program?</h2>
  <p>Ready stock helps a brand test an existing shape without first developing a new pattern. Fitclo's linked set listings show a starting MOQ of 50 sets, but stock, sizes, colors and branding scope must be checked for each style. A custom program is appropriate when your brand needs a specific inseam, waistband, top support, fabric or original color placement. Custom development adds sampling and approval steps, so request a project-specific MOQ and timeline rather than borrowing numbers from a ready-stock listing.</p>
  <p>For both routes, ask for a sample of the exact style and material you plan to sell. Use the sample to check whether the waistband rolls during floor work, whether the top shifts when arms move overhead, and whether lighter colors remain acceptable under stretch. Keep the approved sample and measurements as the reference for later production and reorders.</p>

  <h2>A practical first-order plan</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose the buyer segment: studio shop, online boutique, fitness brand or wholesale distributor.</li>
    <li>Pick one core set and one alternative silhouette before expanding colors.</li>
    <li>Confirm available sizes, colors, fabric details, MOQ and branding for each exact style code.</li>
    <li>Approve samples on real wearers in the movements the collection is intended for.</li>
    <li>Send a quantity by style, color and size so the supplier can provide a meaningful quotation.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>If you are comparing suppliers, use the same brief and approval criteria for each. This makes sample quality and quotations easier to assess than a vague request for “premium Pilates sets.” For broader product choices, browse <a href="/products/matching-sets/">Fitclo matching sets</a> or describe your design through the <a href="/inquiry/">project inquiry form</a>.</p>
